+
+On the isolated 1.0.0 source, three version-contract tests each failed with the relevant production mutation and passed after restoration. They cover exact full Core version declarations (including prerelease and build metadata), incompatible-client rejection before session admission with a corrected retry, and prompt reporting of the matching server rejection while the transport remains open. A different Desktop UI version is accepted when the declared Core version matches. The App Server mutation failed immediately on an unexpected successful response; the predicted timeout was not observed. The same three tests passed again on the pre-relocation source. These successful reruns are separate from the historical mutation evidence and do not verify the final release executables, Desktop integration, or authenticated OpenAI requests.
+
+Pre-relocation source Windows native context regression: 20 suites, 89 distinct passed tests, zero remaining ignored tests in the selected suites. Final executables and whole-release acceptance remain pending. Coverage includes focus/dependencies, HTTP/WS request projection, policy-reset continuation, cache attribution, stale compaction, persistence failures, cancelled waiters, migration, cold resume, and actual fork/original reads. Network cases use synthetic peers; no live authenticated OpenAI request was run.
+
+Pre-relocation source measurements, limited to local projection/normalization/serialization: 100/1,000/10,000 sources, five warmup pairs and 30 measured pairs per size (180 samples). Request bytes fell from 138,992/1,388,192/13,898,192 to 15,245/140,187/1,391,389 (89.0%/89.9%/90.0%). Median time fell from 3.380/35.120/557.740 ms to 0.470/3.643/54.587 ms; p95 fell from 5.148/39.917/647.491 ms to 0.911/4.894/66.233 ms. Median uses the middle-pair average; p95 uses nearest rank. These measurements exclude model/network latency, total process memory, and sustained app workloads.
+
+The regression runs and measurements above predate moving two `#[cfg(test)]` modules into sibling files. A complete build-input comparison verified that only the two module placements and their required file notices changed; the original test bodies and production bytes reconstruct exactly. Fresh version-contract RED/GREEN demonstrated all three cases, and all four moved daemon tests passed. The AppServer pair uses the r41_initialize target, which includes the unchanged original initialize module; the original all-target GREEN was not run. Protocol and daemon results retain their original source identities, reconciled with the added target by exact input comparison. Final binaries, Desktop checks and publication have separate evidence recorded in the release verification appendix. Historical runs are not reported as executions of the new file layout.
+
+R39/R40 test counts, binaries, checksums, and audit results are historical evidence and do not establish R41 acceptance. Source inspection, logging, a successful build, or an audit alone does not establish that the original runtime problem is resolved.
+
+### Known limitations
+
+The index does not automatically infer task completion, instruction expiry, or semantic relevance. Focus must be selected explicitly; without it, the conservative active-task view can retain unrelated details. User/control/unknown and unclassified roots can accumulate independently of summaries, limiting achievable context reduction. Existing summary compaction is still needed when the active set is too large. Projection selects cached active resident positions, but index policy changes clone metadata and rebuild derived sets; index, audit, retained history and original-store growth remain possible. No total process-memory bound or measured performance improvement is claimed. Required archived originals may need explicit `read`; automatic rehydration is not claimed.
+
+Cache coverage is the latest completed sampling response; compaction/prewarm are not observed. Observation time is a host completion time, not server cache creation. Missing metrics remain unknown; malformed metrics are invalid. Unprovided TTL/expiry cannot establish a cache deadline or per-original cache hit, and cache expiry cannot remove required context.
+
+Original lookup is restricted to the current conversation's authorized store. Ephemeral originals may be truncated or unavailable, and already missing originals cannot be reconstructed. Missing IDs, errors, or disabled retrieval are not successful lookup or proof of absence. Forced reset, automatic authentication, raw fallback, and automatic resending of requests with unknown outcomes are excluded.
+
+Pre-relocation source local resume/fork, concurrent compaction and persistence-failure tests passed within the 20 selected suites; final executable verification is pending. Downgrade recovery, actual-model summary quality, Desktop integration, physical keyboard/IME/voice, first-time installation, and sustained workloads remain unverified. No claim is made that all GUI delays, memory growth, or crashes are resolved. Broader memory/CodeMode/Core-store/runtime/history/QSC/cache/refactoring/multi-vendor work is deferred to R42.
