+
+Historical source tests retain their original revision: 20 suites, 89 distinct tests and 180 paired projection samples. Exact input comparisons cover the subsequent two test-module relocations, added initialize wrapper and license-only metadata change. They are not reruns of the final file layout. Fresh targeted version-contract RED/GREEN and four moved daemon tests are separate evidence. Local HTTP/WebSocket tests exercise actual product serialization/authentication/error code against synthetic providers; live authenticated OpenAI account/model execution was NOT_RUN. Projection measurements cover local projection/normalization/serialization only, not model quality, network latency or total process memory.
+
+Core 1.0.0 and every subsequent project version use AGPL-3.0-or-later. The complete ZIP supplies the exact project source plus 493 dependency/native source-and-notice files (667,579,909 bytes before ZIP compression), including all 1,296 locked registry packages, nine Cargo Git repositories, 19 native submodules, the exact Windows V8 producer sources/patch, 11 pinned voice archives and matching unchanged helper/ripgrep source materials. The source-delivery manifest SHA-256 is `e631e6c188b813a90a137e90e0c9fbd05fa4f627541d0b626c5d2d7711e44de1`; package-receipt SHA-256 is `6d300900e688961541a3ceebdbf36919c93e97538166c952e93d6baab4cfd4a8`. Run `python restore.py --verify-only` inside `source/dependencies/` before restoring sources into a new directory. Original Apache, Microsoft and all other component notices retain their own terms. Shared GLib/GStreamer libraries retain LGPL source, replacement and debugging rights. Microsoft CRT redistribution is separate from the project AGPL. See the included bilingual source README and component notices. See also the [component license elections](1.0.0-licensing.md).
